    "title": "U.S. Open Mixed Doubles Final Highlights",
    "text": "• The mixed doubles title match took place at Arthur Ashe Stadium during the U.S. Open.\n• The final three matches featured mainly top singles players for the first time.\n• Italians Sara Errani and Andrea Vavasorri won the mixed doubles championship.\n• The format change for the tournament sparked conversation and controversy.\n• Most players expressed positive feedback about the new format.\n• Jessica Pegula described the atmosphere as 'arguably more crazy' than during singles matches.\n• Jack Draper stated he enjoyed the experience more than expected.\n• Errani and Vavasorri acknowledged the special experience of playing in front of a large crowd.\n• The Italian duo defeated Iga Swiatek and Casper Ruud in the final match.\n• Casper Ruud thanked the tournament for the opportunity to try doubles.\n• The future of the mixed doubles format at other Grand Slam tournaments remains uncertain.\n• Christian Harrison expressed hope for continuing the excitement generated by the event.",
